// ============================================================================
// 05 - Timestamp / timezone sanity check
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose : NOT an investigation query - a diagnostic. Confirms how
//           TimeGenerated is really stored and rendered before you trust any
//           timeline. Log Analytics stores UTC; the portal may display your
//           local timezone, which silently shifts every window you write.
// Use it  : whenever a window "should" have data and comes back empty, or
//           when correlating App Service logs with another system's clock.
//           `affiche` = as the UI renders it, `en_texte` = the raw UTC value.
//           If they differ, your datetime() filters are in UTC, not local time.
// Table   : AppServiceHTTPLogs
//
// TUNABLES:
//   datetime window     -> any 1-2 minute window you know has traffic
//   To convert for reading, add:
//     | extend heure_paris = datetime_utc_to_local(TimeGenerated, "Europe/Paris")
//   NOTE: filter in UTC, convert only for display. Never filter on the
//         converted column - it defeats the ingestion-time index.
// ============================================================================
AppServiceHTTPLogs
| where TimeGenerated between (datetime(2026-09-02 02:14) .. datetime(2026-09-02 02:16))
| extend affiche = TimeGenerated, en_texte = tostring(TimeGenerated)
| project affiche, en_texte, CIp, CsUriStem
